E('elude','/ɪˈluːd/；英亦 /ɪˈljuːd/','逃开；躲过；使想不起或得不到','人或答案都像从手指间溜走：你追、找或回想，却抓不住。','拉丁 eludere 来自 e- 向外 + ludere 玩、戏弄；由躲开、使对方落空发展到逃脱和难以掌握。',ELUD+[['拉丁 eludere → 英语 elude','逃开追捕；也使理解、记忆或追求落空']],'elude capture 是逃过抓捕；His name eludes me 是一时想不起他的名字；success eludes someone 是始终没能成功。','elude capture；elude detection；the answer eludes me；success eluded them。','avoid 通常说主动避开；elude 也可把名字、答案当主语。allude to 则是间接提到，别因读音相近混用。',('The fox eluded the dogs by slipping through a gap in the fence.','狐狸钻过围栏缝隙，躲开了猎犬。'),('The exact word I need still eludes me.','我想用的那个准确词语还是想不起来。'),sources=['https://www.etymonline.com/word/elude','https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elude#English']),
E('elusive','/ɪˈluːsɪv/','难以找到的；难以捉摸的；难以实现的','总像差一点就抓到了，却又从眼前或脑中滑走。','拉丁 eludere 的分词词干 elus- + -ive；与 elude 同源，重音在第二音节。',ELUSIVE,'an elusive animal 很难找到；an elusive meaning 难以捉摸；an elusive victory 是迟迟争取不到的胜利。对象可以真实存在，只是难以得到。','remain elusive；prove elusive；an elusive goal；an elusive concept。','illusory 是表象不真实；elusive 是难以把握。allusive 则是包含暗指的，三个词的重点各不同。',('A permanent solution has remained elusive.','一个长久有效的解决办法仍然难以找到。'),('The photographer spent weeks searching for the elusive bird.','摄影师花了数周寻找那种难觅踪影的鸟。'),sources=['https://www.oxfordlearnersdictionaries.com/definition/english/elusive','https://www.etymonline.com/word/elusive']),
E('elusively','/ɪˈluːsɪvli/','难以捉摸地；难以把握地','已经有一点感觉，却无法清楚捕捉、界定或说出来。','elusive + -ly；把难以抓住的性质用于描述呈现或行动方式。',ELUSIVE+[['英语 elusive + -ly → elusively','难以把握的 → 以难以把握的方式']],'elusively familiar 可形容似曾相识、又想不起来源的感觉。偏书面；说人故意回避回答时，evasively 往往更直接。','elusively familiar；elusively subtle；remain elusively out of reach。','vaguely 说模糊、不明确；elusively 更强调你试图把握它，却始终抓不牢。',('The melody sounded elusively familiar, but she could not name the song.','旋律听着似曾相识，她却怎么也说不出歌名。'),('The scent was elusively subtle, appearing and fading as the breeze changed.','香气若有若无，随着微风变化时隐时现。'),sources=['https://www.oxfordlearnersdictionaries.com/definition/english/elusively','https://www.etymonline.com/word/elusive']),
E('elusiveness','/ɪˈluːsɪvnəs/','难以捉摸；难以捕获或实现的特性','让人觉得总差一步，却始终不能真正抓住的那种性质。','elusive + -ness；把难以寻找、定义或实现这一性质名词化。',ELUSIVE+[['英语 elusive + -ness → elusiveness','难以把握的 → 难以把握这种性质']],'the elusiveness of memory 说记忆难以准确捕捉；the animal’s elusiveness 说动物难觅踪影。通常不可数。','the elusiveness of；an animal’s elusiveness；the elusiveness of success。','difficulty 只说困难；elusiveness 更像抓不住移动的目标，或无法把模糊的东西说准。',('The poem explores the elusiveness of childhood memories.','这首诗探讨童年记忆难以准确捕捉的特点。'),('The animal’s elusiveness makes reliable population counts difficult.','这种动物难觅踪影，使可靠的数量统计很困难。'),sources=['https://www.oxfordlearnersdictionaries.com/definition/english/elusiveness','https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elusiveness#English']),
E('ludicrous','/ˈluːdɪkrəs/；英亦 /ˈljuːdɪkrəs/','荒唐可笑的','离现实、常理或合理比例太远，让人觉得简直像个笑话。','借拉丁 ludicrus 嬉戏的，接 ludere 玩；英语从与玩乐有关转为荒唐到可笑。',LUDICROUS,'a ludicrous claim 是荒唐的说法；a ludicrous price 是高得或低得离谱的价格。语气较强，常用于明确否定。','a ludicrous suggestion；a ludicrous claim；sound ludicrous。','funny 可以只是好笑；ludicrous 常带批评，认为某事不值得认真接受。',('It is ludicrous to expect one person to finish this in an hour.','指望一个人在一小时内做完这件事，太荒唐了。'),('The film turns a ludicrous premise into an entertaining story.','电影把一个荒诞的设定拍成了有趣的故事。'),sources=['https://www.etymonline.com/word/ludicrous','https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ludicrous#English']),
E('ludicrously','/ˈluːdɪkrəsli/；英亦 /ˈljuːdɪkrəsli/','荒唐地；离谱地','某个程度大到或小到失去合理比例，像在开玩笑。','ludicrous + -ly；既可修饰行为，也常放在 expensive、small 等形容词前加强评价。',LUDICROUS+[['英语 ludicrous + -ly → ludicrously','荒唐可笑的 → 以荒唐方式或达到离谱程度']],'ludicrously expensive 是贵得离谱；ludicrously small 是小得不像话。它不只是客观地说非常，而是加上不合理的评价。','ludicrously expensive；ludicrously small；ludicrously exaggerated。','extremely 主要加强程度；ludicrously 还带有荒唐、不成比例的判断。',('The replacement part was ludicrously expensive.','那个替换零件贵得离谱。'),('He arrived with a ludicrously small umbrella for three people.','他带来一把小得离谱的伞，却打算让三个人一起撑。'),sources=['https://www.oxfordlearnersdictionaries.com/definition/english/ludicrously','https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ludicrously#English']),
